          ":question/id": "0c320bbb-0961-56b0-99e4-beaa75aa8f10",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142358",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$ is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement \u201c$A$ is  invertible\u201d is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$ is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$ only."
        },
